This could have been less than 10000 turns, but TDT, in its infinite 
wisdom, recently decided that confused scrolls of teleportation should no 
longer provide reliable level teleporting.  Next time I am simply going 
to curse a big stack of them.

There were no bones files this game, and not much of note in Minetown 
besides a BOH.  Minesend was the spellbook version.  A random uncursed 
amulet (those are safe to wear) turned out to be reflection.  A huge ring 
store around level 10 provided nearly every type of ring, although I was 
only able to sink-identify half.

A throne room at level 15 let me wish for the Eye.  Honestly, it is the 
best item in the game.  Even if you don't spellcast (but you should), the 
power regeneration allows frequent teleportation, and the gate ability is 
a huge time saver.  Oh yes, magic resistance.

I had found a wand of polymorph so I immediately gated back to my stash 
in Sokoban.  The wand gave out after 6 zaps but by then I had most 
spells, including identify.

I gated back to level 15, then dug down to the castle.  Ring of conflict 
and spell of magic missile made it pretty easy.  The wand was 0:3

Helm of brilliance
Spellbook of polymorph
scroll of charging
a cursed marker
a blessed marker
a cursed marker

Smoky potions were full healing, so I eventually alchemized for those and 
got two more wishes, for cursed potions of gain level.

In the past I have zapped Master Kaen with polymorph, as a poor man's 
finger of death, but this time I used teleport to scatter him and the 
items over the map.  Of course he teleported to them and picked them up.  
I wasn't making any progress in melee, so I used spell of drain life to 
slowly kill him.

Izchak only had 5 candles, and none turned up on the polypile.  So I 
spent the final wand wish on them.

Yeenoghu turned up in the graveyard in the sanctum level.  As expected, 
he teleported to the HP and retrieved the amulet.  I beat on him and 
chased him upstairs for a few levels (he did get thrown backwards once).  
But I got bored so I killed him.

The c!oGL were nice; I saved the final one for Medusa's level.

On Astral I went directly to Famine's altar.  



